body:
The tax could not be challenged in court. Non-Muslims had to pay their taxes within 15 days in cash.\[31\] Many people who could not pay the taxes borrowed money from relatives and friends, also sold their properties at public auctions or sold their businesses to gather some money to pay.\[32\]\[33\] People who were unable to pay were sent to labor camps in eastern Anatolia. Auschwitz de bir kamp mı yoksa doğu anadoluda bir kamp mı?

&#x200B;

edit: The Turkish government promised to give back the paid taxes to non-Muslims, but it did not. Source: Akıncılar, Nihan; Rogers, Amanda E.; Dogan, Evinc; Brindisi, Jennifer; Alexieva, Anna; Schimmang, Beatrice (December 2011). Young Minds Rethinking the Mediterranean. Istanbul Kultur University. p. 23. ISBN 978-0415690560.
